---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro'

const title = 'About Zyankov.eu | Zlatko Yankov'
const description = 'Zyankov.eu is a collection of small, practical browser tools by Zlatko Yankov, a frontend engineer from Sofia, Bulgaria.'
const jsonLd = {
  '@type': 'AboutPage',
  mainEntity: {
    '@type': 'Person',
    name: 'Zlatko Yankov',
    jobTitle: 'Frontend engineer',
    address: { '@type': 'PostalAddress', addressLocality: 'Sofia', addressCountry: 'BG' },
    email: 'mailto:hello@zyankov.eu',
    url: 'https://zyankov.eu/about/',
  },
}
---

<PageLayout title={title} description={description} path="/about/" alternates={{ en: '/about/', bg: '/bg/za-saita/' }} noAds={false} project="about" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Hi, I’m Zlatko.</h1>
      <p class="intro">
        Zyankov.eu is where I publish small, practical tools that run in your browser. I’m Zlatko Yankov, a frontend engineer from Sofia, Bulgaria, and I build and maintain every project on this site myself.
      </p>

      <section>
        <h2>Who builds these tools</h2>
        <p>For about ten years I have built and maintained web applications. Much of that time went into a large business application: supporting and improving its original AngularJS version, building its Angular successor, and migrating it step by step, release after release, across many Angular versions.</p>
        <p>That kind of work is mostly invisible to the people who use it. Zyankov.eu is the opposite: tools that do one job you can see, built with the same care for correctness, accessibility and maintenance.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What you will find here</h2>
        <p><a href="/letterwell/">Letterwell</a> finds words from a set of letters in English or <a href="/letterwell/bg/">Bulgarian</a> and shows Scrabble, Words With Friends and Boggle scores.</p>
        <p><a href="/letterwell/daily/">Letterwell Daily</a> is a five-letter word game with a new word every day, in English and Bulgarian, with spoiler-free hints.</p>
        <p><a href="/calculators/">BuildCalc</a> estimates materials for home-improvement jobs: concrete, gravel, paint, tile, flooring, drywall, adhesive and grout, screed, wallpaper, insulation and masonry, with guides that explain the assumptions behind each estimate. Bulgarian versions in metres add heating, firewood, air conditioner and electricity calculators, and everyday sums such as VAT, percentages, leva to euro and loan payments. In English there are also <a href="/percentage-calculator/">percentage</a>, <a href="/date-calculator/">date</a> and <a href="/loan-calculator/">loan payment</a> calculators.</p>
        <p>New tools and articles are added over time. Each tool works without an account and is designed to work on phones, tablets and desktops.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>How the tools are made</h2>
        <p>Calculations and word searches run in your browser, so what you type is not sent to a server. Each calculator shows its formula, an example and its limitations, and the calculation code is covered by automated tests.</p>
        <p>Letterwell uses openly licensed (MIT) word lists; see the <a href="/letterwell/english-words-license.txt">English</a> and <a href="/letterwell/bulgarian-words-license.txt">Bulgarian</a> licence notices. Lists can differ from official game dictionaries, so check the rules of the game you are playing.</p>
        <p>When someone reports an error, I fix it and note the change. Reports about accessibility problems are especially welcome.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="sources">
        <h2>Where the numbers come from</h2>
        <p>An estimate is only worth something if you can check it. Every calculator follows the same rules:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>The formula is on the page</strong>, under the calculator, with an explanation of why it works that way.</li>
          <li><strong>Every default figure has a source</strong>: a manufacturer's data sheet (Knauf, Ceresit, Baumit, Wienerberger and others), a standard or regulation, a public institution, or at least a published article. The sources are linked under each calculator.</li>
          <li><strong>Our own estimates are labelled as such</strong>, for example a middle value between several published concrete recipes.</li>
          <li><strong>Prices and figures carry a date</strong> (“checked on …”), because prices and products change.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>If a number has no source, it does not go into a calculator. If you find a figure that does not match the product you are using, enter your own value in the calculator and please tell me, so I can check it.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="changes">
        <h2>Corrections</h2>
        <p>When a figure turns out to be wrong, it is corrected and listed here.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>7 November 2026</strong>: source check of every calculator. Self-levelling compound 1.8 → 1.6 kg/m² per mm and gypsum plaster 0.9 → 1.0 (Ceresit, Baumit, Knauf data sheets); drywall screws 11 → 15 per m² of board (Knauf); exterior insulation adhesive 5.5 → 5.0 kg/m² (Ceresit CT 85); loose ballast 1.8 → 1.6 t/m³; drywall tape and compound in BuildCalc to USG figures; several appliance presets in the electricity calculator.</li>
          <li><strong>7 November 2026</strong>: loose firewood is about 1.5 times the stacked volume, not 1.43 (Bavarian State Institute of Forestry).</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>English and Bulgarian</h2>
        <p>I am Bulgarian, and the site is written in English and Bulgarian. Where a Bulgarian version adds real value, such as Letterwell’s Bulgarian dictionary or calculators in metres with Bulgarian products and prices, it has its own page. <a href="/bg/za-saita/" hreflang="bg" lang="bg">Тази страница на български</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Advertising</h2>
        <p>The site shows ads from Google AdSense, which keeps the tools free. Advertising, consent and analytics are described in the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="contact">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions, corrections and ideas for new tools are welcome at <a href="mailto:hello@zyankov.eu">hello@zyankov.eu</a>. Please mention the page or tool and what you expected to happen; do not send sensitive personal information.</p>
      </section>
</PageLayout>
